    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2004-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(|x - 1|\\) and \\(|x - 2|\\) are the distances from \\(x\\) to \\(1\\) and \\(2,\\) the point \\(x\\) is equidistant from \\(1\\) and \\(2.\\)\n\nThat midpoint is \\[ x = \\dfrac{1 + 2}{2} = \\dfrac{3}{2}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(|x - a|\\) measures the distance from \\(x\\) to \\(a\\)",
        "The point \\(x\\) must be equally far from \\(1\\) and \\(2\\)"
      ],
